raphael: let the MDP/DPU fast paths run on this board (opt-in) and find its SMMU streams

sweetfb_direct and sweetfb_hw/sweetfb_zc never engaged on raphael: the whole
MDP block in SweetFramebuffer::start (mdpProbe, the hardware scaler, page
flipping, the zero-copy/direct scanout setup and the MDP SMMU probe) sits behind
sweet_board_beryllium(), so on SM8150 every boot ended in mode=copy and each
frame went through the 10.9 MB CPU copy.

Both boards share the MDSS window (DSI0 at 0x0ae94000 = 0x0ae00000 + 0x94000),
so the block is now gated by gMdp = beryllium || (raphael && sweetfb_mdp=1).
With sweetfb_mdp=1 alone it only probes: mdpProbe() and the SMMU stream probe
are read-only, and sweetfb_hw/sweetfb_direct/sweetfb_zc still have to be given
before anything is written (the DPU revision on SM8150 is unverified).

raphael-specific data comes as boot args so it can be found from a boot image
instead of a kernel rebuild:
  sweetfb_mdp_pa=0x...   MDP window base (default 0x0ae00000)
  sweetfb_sid_a/sid_b    MDP apps_smmu stream ids (default 0x880/0xc80, sdm845)
  sweetfb_smmu_scan=1    dump every valid SMR/S2CR (new read-only
                         sweet_smmu_dump_smr() in bsd/dev/sweet_smmu.c) so the
                         real MDP stream ids can be read off the phone

Also log stats windows longer than 3 s ("vsync ticks stalled"): win_ms=8901 was
seen on a boot in mode=copy and is the stall the user feels, not a low frame rate.

